{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_9212f413546240b7b332901a","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<canvas id=\"0:1\" name=\"00 · Start Here 设计任务\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\">\n  <frame id=\"3:2\" name=\"Start Here · Brief\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1440\" height=\"2210\">\n    <frame id=\"3:3\" name=\"Header\" x=\"64\" y=\"64\" width=\"1312\" height=\"145\">\n      <text id=\"3:4\" name=\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"182\" height=\"19\" />\n      <text id=\"3:5\" name=\"Deniz Arslan — 3D artist portfolio\" x=\"0\" y=\"31\" width=\"1312\" height=\"52\" />\n      <text id=\"3:6\" name=\"Design a two-page personal portfolio for a 3D artist and sculptor: a work page with three projects and an about page with skills and contact. Desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" x=\"0\" y=\"95\" width=\"1312\" height=\"50\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:7\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"64\" y=\"257\" width=\"1312\" height=\"249\">\n      <text id=\"3:8\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"147\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:9\" name=\"1. Build exactly the 2 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives no Button or Text Field: the source has neither (every action is a text link). Design the header, footer, link style, current-page state and every content block as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the portrait photo and the icons from 04 · Media. The three project images are not supplied in the source — use image placeholders. The logo “da.” is plain text. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"198\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:10\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"64\" y=\"554\" width=\"1312\" height=\"425\">\n      <text id=\"3:11\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"413\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:12\" name=\"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <frame id=\"3:13\" name=\"Frame cards\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"336\">\n        <frame id=\"3:14\" name=\"01_Work\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"336\">\n          <text id=\"3:15\" name=\"01_Work\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"77\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"3:16\" name=\"Goal: See who the artist is and browse three projects.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:17\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"3:18\" name=\"• Footer: “Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020” · Artstation · LinkedIn · Twitter • Header: logo “da.” · navigation Work / About / Playground / Contact · current: Work • Intro: “Hello, I’m Deniz.” · “A senior-year design student who is trying to specialize in 3D modeling &amp; texturing.” · scroll cue (Icon_Arrow_Down) • Projects: 3 project blocks, each with number and name, description, tools line where given, link or status, and an image placeholder (see DATA)\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"120\" />\n          <text id=\"3:19\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"246\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"3:20\" name=\"→ About (nav) → 02_About → logo “da.”, Work (nav) → 01_Work (self)\" x=\"24\" y=\"272\" width=\"596\" height=\"40\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:21\" name=\"02_About\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"336\">\n          <text id=\"3:22\" name=\"02_About\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"87\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"3:23\" name=\"Goal: Learn about the artist’s background and skills, and get in touch.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:24\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"3:25\" name=\"• Contact: “I’d be thrilled to hear about your next project” (Icon_Arrow_Right) · “deniz.arslan@example.com” · “View Resume” • Footer: “Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020” · Artstation · LinkedIn · Twitter • Header: logo “da.” · navigation Work / About / Playground / Contact · current: About • Intro: “Hi, I’m Deniz Arslan, 3D artist &amp; sculptor.” · biography (2 paragraphs, see DATA) · Photo_Profile • Skills: “Main Software” and “Main Skills”, each with its list (see DATA)\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"140\" />\n          <text id=\"3:26\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"266\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"3:27\" name=\"→ logo “da.”, Work (nav) → 01_Work\" x=\"24\" y=\"292\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:28\" name=\"Navigation structure\" x=\"64\" y=\"1027\" width=\"1312\" height=\"117\">\n      <text id=\"3:29\" name=\"Navigation structure\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"242\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:30\" name=\"• Two pages share the header and footer. The current page is shown in the navigation. • Work → 01_Work · About → 02_About · logo “da.” → 01_Work. • Entry only (no frame): Playground, Contact, project links, Artstation / LinkedIn / Twitter, the email address, View Resume.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"66\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:31\" name=\"Fixed data &amp; copy\" x=\"64\" y=\"1192\" width=\"1312\" height=\"347\">\n      <text id=\"3:32\" name=\"Fixed data &amp; copy\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"207\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:33\" name=\"Use these values verbatim.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <frame id=\"3:34\" name=\"Data blocks\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"258\">\n        <frame id=\"3:35\" name=\"Projects (in order)\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"258\">\n          <text id=\"3:36\" name=\"Projects (in order)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:37\" name=\"01 / Goblin Bust — “Goblin concept digital sculpture with human-like skin. Learned a lot of quick tips and look development.” · tools: “Sculpted in ZBrush, retopologized and UV-mapped in Maya, textured in Mari, rendered with Arnold.” · link “More shots from this project ↗” 02 / Skin Shader Study — “Subsurface weight, specular roughness and diffuse maps generated with procedural and manual techniques.” · link “See case study →” 03 / Creature Concept — “Experimental creature modeling for a school project.” · status “Project WIP” (not a link)\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"190\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:38\" name=\"Biography (02_About)\" x=\"444\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"163\">\n          <text id=\"3:39\" name=\"Biography (02_About)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:40\" name=\"“My work is mainly focused on 3D modeling, texturing and rendering. I like exploring creatures with a touch of dark surrealism for characters and production.” “Now I’m an interactive media design student in Istanbul ⏤ currently freelancing and seeking internship opportunities.”\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"95\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:41\" name=\"Skills (02_About)\" x=\"888\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"163\">\n          <text id=\"3:42\" name=\"Skills (02_About)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:43\" name=\"Main Software: Pixologic ZBrush, Autodesk Maya, The Foundry Mari, Arnold Renderer, Blender, Forger · Adobe CC, Figma, Ableton Main Skills: Organic and Polygonal Modeling, UV Layout, Texturing, Retopology, Illustration, Sound Design\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"95\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:44\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"64\" y=\"1587\" width=\"1312\" height=\"252\">\n      <text id=\"3:45\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"328\" height=\"35\" />\n      <frame id=\"3:46\" name=\"Fixed vs yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"201\">\n        <frame id=\"3:47\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"181\">\n          <text id=\"3:48\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"3:49\" name=\"• Frame names and links • Must-include content (what, not how) • All data and copy • Brand colors #181717 and #2429AF, and DM Sans • Media: portrait photo, icons\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"100\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:50\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"201\">\n          <text id=\"3:51\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"197\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"3:52\" name=\"• Layout, grid, grouping, order and emphasis on both pages • All other colors: page background, secondary text, dividers, image placeholders • Type scale, spacing • All states: current page, link hover • Header, footer, link style, project block, skill list, contact block • How the portrait is cropped and placed\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"120\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:53\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"64\" y=\"1887\" width=\"1312\" height=\"259\">\n      <text id=\"3:54\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"222\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:55\" name=\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <text id=\"3:56\" name=\"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data &amp; copy accuracy 3. Flow &amp; prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality &amp; consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse (shared header / footer)\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"132\" />\n      <text id=\"3:57\" name=\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 2 named frames, your components and the prototype.\" x=\"0\" y=\"237\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n    </frame>\n  </frame>\n</canvas>"},{"type":"text","text":"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design, since this tool only returns metadata. If you do not call get_design_context, the agent will not be able to implement the design."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89a64135-6412-4ef4-999c-ac66165ec06a","uuid":"1def3857-a84a-42b7-bf1a-c7c3bf45ecb6","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:18:34.918Z","tool_use_result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<canvas id=\"0:1\" name=\"00 · Start Here 设计任务\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\">\n  <frame id=\"3:2\" name=\"Start Here · Brief\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1440\" height=\"2210\">\n    <frame id=\"3:3\" name=\"Header\" x=\"64\" y=\"64\" width=\"1312\" height=\"145\">\n      <text id=\"3:4\" name=\"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"182\" height=\"19\" />\n      <text id=\"3:5\" name=\"Deniz Arslan — 3D artist portfolio\" x=\"0\" y=\"31\" width=\"1312\" height=\"52\" />\n      <text id=\"3:6\" name=\"Design a two-page personal portfolio for a 3D artist and sculptor: a work page with three projects and an about page with skills and contact. Desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" x=\"0\" y=\"95\" width=\"1312\" height=\"50\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:7\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"64\" y=\"257\" width=\"1312\" height=\"249\">\n      <text id=\"3:8\" name=\"How to work\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"147\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:9\" name=\"1. Build exactly the 2 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The two brand colors and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives no Button or Text Field: the source has neither (every action is a text link). Design the header, footer, link style, current-page state and every content block as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the portrait photo and the icons from 04 · Media. The three project images are not supplied in the source — use image placeholders. The logo “da.” is plain text. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"198\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:10\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"64\" y=\"554\" width=\"1312\" height=\"425\">\n      <text id=\"3:11\" name=\"Frames · goals · must include · links\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"413\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:12\" name=\"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <frame id=\"3:13\" name=\"Frame cards\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"336\">\n        <frame id=\"3:14\" name=\"01_Work\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"336\">\n          <text id=\"3:15\" name=\"01_Work\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"77\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"3:16\" name=\"Goal: See who the artist is and browse three projects.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:17\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"3:18\" name=\"• Footer: “Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020” · Artstation · LinkedIn · Twitter • Header: logo “da.” · navigation Work / About / Playground / Contact · current: Work • Intro: “Hello, I’m Deniz.” · “A senior-year design student who is trying to specialize in 3D modeling &amp; texturing.” · scroll cue (Icon_Arrow_Down) • Projects: 3 project blocks, each with number and name, description, tools line where given, link or status, and an image placeholder (see DATA)\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"120\" />\n          <text id=\"3:19\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"246\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"3:20\" name=\"→ About (nav) → 02_About → logo “da.”, Work (nav) → 01_Work (self)\" x=\"24\" y=\"272\" width=\"596\" height=\"40\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:21\" name=\"02_About\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"336\">\n          <text id=\"3:22\" name=\"02_About\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"87\" height=\"26\" />\n          <text id=\"3:23\" name=\"Goal: Learn about the artist’s background and skills, and get in touch.\" x=\"24\" y=\"60\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:24\" name=\"MUST INCLUDE\" x=\"24\" y=\"90\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"3:25\" name=\"• Contact: “I’d be thrilled to hear about your next project” (Icon_Arrow_Right) · “deniz.arslan@example.com” · “View Resume” • Footer: “Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020” · Artstation · LinkedIn · Twitter • Header: logo “da.” · navigation Work / About / Playground / Contact · current: About • Intro: “Hi, I’m Deniz Arslan, 3D artist &amp; sculptor.” · biography (2 paragraphs, see DATA) · Photo_Profile • Skills: “Main Software” and “Main Skills”, each with its list (see DATA)\" x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"596\" height=\"140\" />\n          <text id=\"3:26\" name=\"LINKS\" x=\"24\" y=\"266\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" />\n          <text id=\"3:27\" name=\"→ logo “da.”, Work (nav) → 01_Work\" x=\"24\" y=\"292\" width=\"596\" height=\"20\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:28\" name=\"Navigation structure\" x=\"64\" y=\"1027\" width=\"1312\" height=\"117\">\n      <text id=\"3:29\" name=\"Navigation structure\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"242\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:30\" name=\"• Two pages share the header and footer. The current page is shown in the navigation. • Work → 01_Work · About → 02_About · logo “da.” → 01_Work. • Entry only (no frame): Playground, Contact, project links, Artstation / LinkedIn / Twitter, the email address, View Resume.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"66\" />\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:31\" name=\"Fixed data &amp; copy\" x=\"64\" y=\"1192\" width=\"1312\" height=\"347\">\n      <text id=\"3:32\" name=\"Fixed data &amp; copy\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"207\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:33\" name=\"Use these values verbatim.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <frame id=\"3:34\" name=\"Data blocks\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"258\">\n        <frame id=\"3:35\" name=\"Projects (in order)\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"258\">\n          <text id=\"3:36\" name=\"Projects (in order)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:37\" name=\"01 / Goblin Bust — “Goblin concept digital sculpture with human-like skin. Learned a lot of quick tips and look development.” · tools: “Sculpted in ZBrush, retopologized and UV-mapped in Maya, textured in Mari, rendered with Arnold.” · link “More shots from this project ↗” 02 / Skin Shader Study — “Subsurface weight, specular roughness and diffuse maps generated with procedural and manual techniques.” · link “See case study →” 03 / Creature Concept — “Experimental creature modeling for a school project.” · status “Project WIP” (not a link)\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"190\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:38\" name=\"Biography (02_About)\" x=\"444\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"163\">\n          <text id=\"3:39\" name=\"Biography (02_About)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:40\" name=\"“My work is mainly focused on 3D modeling, texturing and rendering. I like exploring creatures with a touch of dark surrealism for characters and production.” “Now I’m an interactive media design student in Istanbul ⏤ currently freelancing and seeking internship opportunities.”\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"95\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:41\" name=\"Skills (02_About)\" x=\"888\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"163\">\n          <text id=\"3:42\" name=\"Skills (02_About)\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />\n          <text id=\"3:43\" name=\"Main Software: Pixologic ZBrush, Autodesk Maya, The Foundry Mari, Arnold Renderer, Blender, Forger · Adobe CC, Figma, Ableton Main Skills: Organic and Polygonal Modeling, UV Layout, Texturing, Retopology, Illustration, Sound Design\" x=\"20\" y=\"48\" width=\"380\" height=\"95\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:44\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"64\" y=\"1587\" width=\"1312\" height=\"252\">\n      <text id=\"3:45\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"328\" height=\"35\" />\n      <frame id=\"3:46\" name=\"Fixed vs yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"201\">\n        <frame id=\"3:47\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"181\">\n          <text id=\"3:48\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"3:49\" name=\"• Frame names and links • Must-include content (what, not how) • All data and copy • Brand colors #181717 and #2429AF, and DM Sans • Media: portrait photo, icons\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"100\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:50\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"201\">\n          <text id=\"3:51\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"197\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"3:52\" name=\"• Layout, grid, grouping, order and emphasis on both pages • All other colors: page background, secondary text, dividers, image placeholders • Type scale, spacing • All states: current page, link hover • Header, footer, link style, project block, skill list, contact block • How the portrait is cropped and placed\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"120\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:53\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"64\" y=\"1887\" width=\"1312\" height=\"259\">\n      <text id=\"3:54\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"222\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"3:55\" name=\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <text id=\"3:56\" name=\"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data &amp; copy accuracy 3. Flow &amp; prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality &amp; consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse (shared header / footer)\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"132\" />\n      <text id=\"3:57\" name=\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 2 named frames, your components and the prototype.\" x=\"0\" y=\"237\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n    </frame>\n  </frame>\n</canvas>"},{"type":"text","text":"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design, since this tool only returns metadata. If you do not call get_design_context, the agent will not be able to implement the design."}],"_meta":{"mcpRequestId":"f370b23f-ab48-474b-8d69-b43c484cb53a"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_9212f413546240b7b332901a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
