Each call is separate execution context; variables don't persist). So define helpers each call.\n\nLet me now also verify the Photo_Profile: 2:5 is 228×320 inside frame 2:11. Is 2:5 a COMPONENT? If INSTANCE, mainComponent may be a component that lives... somewhere (maybe defined on Media page itself — the <symbol> in XML usually = component master; instances show as <instance> in real Figma XML; here everything is \"symbol\"/\"rounded-rectangle\"/\"vector\"/\"frame\"/\"text\" simplified). I'll handle both at runtime.\n\nAlso icon recolor: master icon = frame (24×24) containing vector with fill #1A1A1F. Recolor: for each descendant with fills, set to ink? Vectors may have stroke instead of fill. Set both fills and strokes? If vector uses stroke, recolor stroke. I'll iterate: for each child vector: if fills && fills !== figma.mixed → set fill ink; if strokes length → set stroke ink. Careful: icon might be filled path (arrow shapes are usually filled). I'll set fills to ink if fills not empty/mixed.\n\nIcons needed in accent color (in Text Link / Contact): instance fill override on vector child inside instance — allowed: instance.findChildren... modify fills of instance child = override. OK.\n\nAlternatively keep icons ink; links accent text + ink icon? Blue icon matches link. I'll override to accent on instances inside components (Text Link, Contact).\n\nNow the ⏤ char and ’ and & — set via JS strings; ensure JSON escaping fine.\n\nText creation helper:\n```js\nasync function T(chars, size, style, color, opts={}){\n  await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"DM Sans\", style});\n  const t = figma.createText();\n  t.fontName = {family:\"DM Sans\", style};\n  t.characters = chars;\n  t.fontSize = size;\n  if(opts.lh) t.lineHeight = {value: opts.lh, unit:\"PIXELS\"};\n  if(opts.ls !== undefined) t.letterSpacing = {value: opts.ls, unit:\"PERCENT\"};\n  t.fills = [solid(color)];\n  ...\n}\n```\nLoad all fonts once at start of each call (Regular, Medium, Bold).\n\nColors:\n```js\nconst C = {\n ink:{r:24/255,g:23/255,b:23/255},\n accent:{r:36/255,g:41/255,b:175/255},\n secondary:{r:111/255,g:107/255,b:102/255}, // #6F6B66\n muted:{r:152/255,g:147/255,b:140/255},    // #98938C\n divider:{r:231/255,g:228/255,b:224/255},  // #E7E4E0\n placeholder:{r:237/255,g:234/255,b:230/255},// #EDEAE6\n subtle:{r:246/255,g:244/255,b:241/255},   // #F6F4F1\n bg:{r:1,g:1,b:1}\n};\n```\n\nAuto-layout API notes:\n- frame.layoutMode = \"VERTICAL\"; frame.primaryAxisSizingMode = \"AUTO\" (hug) or \"FIXED\"; counterAxisSizingMode similarly.\n- itemSpacing; paddingLeft/Right/Top/Bottom.\n- primaryAxisAlignItems: \"MIN\"|\"MAX\"|\"CENTER\"|\"SPACE_BETWEEN\"; counterAxisAlignItems: \"MIN\"|\"CENTER\"|\"MAX\"|\"BASELINE\".\n- child.layoutAlign = \"STRETCH\" for cross-axis fill (works when parent auto-layout; note: layoutAlign STRETCH with counterAxisSizingMode AUTO parent? It works: child stretches).\n- For width-fill text (paragraphs): parent VERTICAL, child.layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\" + textAutoResize default? Text node in auto-layout: set textAutoResize = \"HEIGHT\" and layoutAlign STRETCH → width fills, height auto. Yes.\n\nFor name row baseline: counterAxisAlignItems = \"BASELINE\".\n\nOrder of setting: create frame, set layoutMode, sizing, then append children.\n\nComponent creation: const comp = figma.createComponent(); set size/layout; add children. For variants: comp.addComponentProperty(\"State\",\"VARIANT\",\"Default\")? Variant properties: created via figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, parent) then the ComponentSetNode; variant props defined by node names \"State=Default\". Workflow: create multiple ComponentNodes named \"State=Default\", \"State=Hover\" etc., then figma.combineAsVariants([c1,c2,...], page). The combineAsVariants gives ComponentSetNode. Variant naming: component.name = \"Current=No, State=Default\".\n\nFor NavLink 4 variants: names: \"Current=No, State=Default\", \"Current=No, State=Hover\", \"Current=Yes, State=Default\", \"Current=Yes, State=Hover\". combineAsVariants sorts them.\n\ncreateInstance from a variant: variantComp.createInstance() — yes, instances of specific variant. setProperties({\"Current\":\"Yes\"}) etc.\n\nHover wiring: on each variant master, reactions = [{trigger:{type:\"MouseEnter\"}, action:{type:\"CHANGE_TO\", destinationId: hoverVariantId}}]. And on hover variants MouseLeave → default variant.\n\nWait, CHANGE_TO on an instance switches its variant — destination is variant node id. OK.\n\nText Link 6 variants: \"Icon=None, State=Default\", \"Icon=None, State=Hover\", \"Icon=ArrowRight, State=Default\", \"Icon=ArrowRight, State=Hover\", \"Icon=ArrowUpRight, State=Default\", \"Icon=ArrowUpRight, State=Hover\".\n\nProject Block 2 variants: \"CTA=Link\", \"CTA=Status\".\n\nTotal components: NavLink set, TextLink set, Header, Footer, ImagePlaceholder, ProjectBlock set, SkillList (single, overrides), ContactBlock, + media clones (Photo, 3 icons). \n\nMedia clones: clone masters into workspace page. figma.clone(node) — clone of component = component. Position them. Then use createInstance.\n\nHmm wait: cloning 2:5 (Photo) — if 2:5 is INSTANCE, clone yields instance; I need master: n.mainComponent, then clone master. If master lives on Media page, cloning master to workspace duplicates it. Then instances from the clone.\n\nBut careful: \"Copy these components into your own file and use them as instances\" — within same file, cloning masters to workspace = copied. Good. Keep Media page untouched (clone doesn't modify source).\n\nNow, page frames content details:\n\n**01_Work:**\n```\nFrame 01_Work: VERTICAL, width 1440 FIXED, hug height, fill bg white, itemSpacing 0, clipsContent true? name \"01_Work\".\n├ Header instance (stretch, Current=Yes on \"Work\")\n├ Intro: VERTICAL padding: top 96, sides 80, bottom 120; gap 32; stretch\n│  ├ \"Hello, I'm Deniz.\" 64 Bold ink lh 72\n│  ├ para 20/30 secondary width 620 (textAutoResize HEIGHT, layoutAlign MIN with fixed width? For fixed-width text in auto-layout: set text width via resize(620, h) with textAutoResize \"HEIGHT\", layoutAlign \"MIN\")\n│  └ ArrowDown icon instance 24 ink (maybe margin-top 8)\n├ Projects: VERTICAL padding 0 80 0 80, gap 80, bottom padding 140? set paddingBottom 140; stretch\n│  ├ PB1 (Link variant) overrides: num \"01\", name \"Goblin Bust\", desc \"Goblin concept digital sculpture with human-like skin. Learned a lot of quick tips and look development.\", tools visible text \"Sculpted in ZBrush, retopologized and UV-mapped in Maya, textured in Mari, rendered with Arnold.\", link text \"More shots from this project\" icon UpRight\n│  ├ Divider (stretch h1)\n│  ├ PB2 (Link): \"02\" \"Skin Shader Study\" desc \"Subsurface weight, specular roughness and diffuse maps generated with procedural and manual techniques.\" tools hidden, link \"See case study\" icon Right\n│  ├ Divider\n│  └ PB3 (Status): \"03\" \"Creature Concept\" desc \"Experimental creature modeling for a school project.\" tools hidden, badge \"Project WIP\"\n└ Footer instance (stretch)\n```\n\nProject number styling: \"01\" accent Medium 16? and name 26 Medium. Row baseline: \"01 / Goblin Bust\": nodes: \"01\" (16 Medium accent), \"/\" (16 Medium muted), name (26 Medium ink). Hmm baseline align across different sizes — BASELINE alignment works in horizontal auto-layout. Good.\n\nActually visually nicer: number ghost large: \"01\" 64 Bold with color #E7E4E0 (very light) behind name? Editorial style. Let me do: Row baseline: \"01\" (64 Bold, color placeholder-ish #DDD9D4) + name \"Goblin Bust\" (26 Medium ink). The \"/\" — data \"01 / Goblin Bust\" — include \"/\"? If I do \"01\" then \"/\" then name, with 64px number the slash looks odd. Copy accuracy: number and name present; separator is notation. I'll include all three tokens: \"01\" big ghost, \"/\" 26 muted, name 26 ink — baseline aligned. Looks designed.\n\nHmm, big 64 number next to 26 name baseline-aligned looks fine (like index). \n\nTools line: prefix label \"Tools — \"? Data: 'tools: \"Sculpted in ZBrush, ...\"'. Render: label \"Tools\" 11 uppercase muted + text? Keep simple: small text \"Sculpted in ZBrush, retopologized and UV-mapped in Maya, textured in Mari, rendered with Arnold.\" 14/22 muted. Fine.\n\nLink: Text Link instance: text override \"More shots from this project\", icon UpRight (accent). Instance variant \"Icon=ArrowUpRight\". Override text: instance.children[0] = text? Text Link structure: [text, icon?]. Overriding text characters on instance child: allowed.\n\nEmail/View Resume font size 20 override on instance (fontSize override allowed).\n\n**02_About:**\n```\nFrame 02_About: VERTICAL width 1440 hug height\n├ Header instance (About Current=Yes)\n├ Hero: VERTICAL padding 96 80 120 80; gap 0\n│  └ Row: HORIZONTAL gap 120 counterAlign MIN stretch\n│     ├ LeftCol VERTICAL gap 40 (stretch/width 720)\n│     │  ├ \"Hi, I'm Deniz Arslan, 3D artist & sculptor.\" 56/64 Bold ink width 720\n│     │  └ Bio VERTICAL gap 20: P1, P2 (16/26 secondary width 560)\n│     └ Photo instance (228×320 → rescale 420/228=1.8421 → 420×589.5)\n├ Skills: VERTICAL padding 0 80 120 80 gap 40 stretch? two SkillLists row:\n│  └ Row HORIZONTAL gap 32 stretch: SL1 (\"Main Software\"), SL2 (\"Main Skills\") each stretch 624\n├ Contact: padding 0 80 140 80: ContactBlock instance stretch\n└ Footer instance\n```\n\nWait contact needs bottom padding before footer; Contact section padding bottom 140.\n\nSkill List width: stretch → equal widths 624 each.\n\nSkillList rows: for Software: 6 rows; Skills: 6 rows. \n\nMain Software rows:\n1. Pixologic ZBrush\n2. Autodesk Maya\n3. The Foundry Mari\n4. Arnold Renderer\n5. Blender\n6. Forger · Adobe CC, Figma, Ableton\n\nMain Skills rows:\n1. Organic and Polygonal Modeling\n2. UV Layout\n3. Texturing\n4. Retopology\n5. Illustration\n6. Sound Design\n\nRow style: 17/24 ink? 16 Regular ink, padding TB 14. Divider between rows. Title \"Main Software\" 12 Medium uppercase ls 8% muted, bottom margin 12, and maybe a divider under title? Title then divider then rows.\n\n**Prototype wiring (Call H):**\n- Frame ids: 01_Work = W, 02_About = A.\n- In W header instance: find text \"Work\" nav instance (NavLink instance containing text \"Work\") — the NavLink instance node; set reactions on... the NavLink instance itself (instance-level reaction? Setting reactions on the instance node — allowed? reactions on InstanceNode: I think yes? Prototype connections on component instances: In UI you can link an entire instance. reactions setter on instance: docs say reactions settable on nodes that can have interactions — instances can. I'll try instance node first, fallback to its inner text child, fallback hotspot rect.)\n  - About instance → NODE 02_About NAVIGATE\n  - Work instance → NODE 01_Work\n  - logo text (inside header instance, it's a plain text child of header master → in instance it's an override-able child; set reactions on it) → NODE 01_Work\n- Same in A: Work → 01_Work; logo → 01_Work; About → 02_About? Not listed; skip. Hmm — but then on About page, \"About\" nav has no action; fine per brief.\n- ArrowDown icon in W: SCROLL_TO first Project Block instance? SCROLL_TO action destination any node. Set on the icon instance in W → scroll to Projects section frame. Trigger Click. (Optional extra; brief lists scroll cue as content only. I'll add it — enhances flow without conflicting.)\n\nWait, also — is there a \"Playground\"/\"Contact\" nav action? \"Entry only (no frame)\" — no action. OK.\n\n**Hotspot fallback:** compute target node absoluteBoundingBox relative to page frame; create rect in page frame (page frame is auto-layout though — adding rect child would enter layout!). Auto-layout frames position children via layout — can't free-position hotspot inside. Solution: hotspot rect appended to page frame with layoutPositioning = \"ABSOLUTE\" (supported in auto-layout: child.layoutPositioning = \"ABSOLUTE\", then x/y relative to frame). Yes! layoutPositioning ABSOLUTE works