ite the code for Call A now. Also I want the photo's natural size confirmed (228×320).\n\nAlso check DM Sans styles availability: try loading Regular, Medium, Bold; if a style fails, record. Bold needed for logo/headings; Medium for nav/labels.\n\nCode Call A:\n\n```js\nconst ws = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"4:2\");\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(ws);\nconst need = [[\"DM Sans\",\"Regular\"],[\"DM Sans\",\"Medium\"],[\"DM Sans\",\"Bold\"]];\nconst loaded=[], failed=[];\nfor(const [f,s] of need){try{await figma.loadFontAsync({family:f,style:s});loaded.push(f+\"/\"+s);}catch(e){failed.push(f+\"/\"+s);}}\n\nfunction solid(c,opacity=1){return {type:\"SOLID\",color:c,opacity};}\nconst INK={r:24/255,g:23/255,b:23/255};\n\nasync function resolveMaster(id){\n  const n=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  if(!n) return null;\n  return n.type===\"INSTANCE\"? n.mainComponent : n;\n}\nconst out={};\nconst media={photo:[\"2:5\",(1560,580)]...}\n```\n\nJS syntax: object with tuples. Write plainly.\n\n```js\nconst specs=[\n {key:\"photo\", id:\"2:5\", x:1560, y:580, name:\"Photo_Profile\"},\n {key:\"down\", id:\"2:2\", x:1560, y:980, name:\"Icon_Arrow_Down\"},\n {key:\"right\", id:\"2:3\", x:1620, y:980, name:\"Icon_Arrow_Right\"},\n {key:\"upright\", id:\"2:4\", x:1680, y:980, name:\"Icon_Arrow_Up_Right\"},\n];\nfor(const s of specs){\n  const m=await resolveMaster(s.id);\n  if(!m){out[s.key]=\"MISSING \"+s.id; continue;}\n  const c=m.clone();\n  ws.appendChild(c);\n  c.name=s.name;\n  c.x=s.x; c.y=s.y;\n  if(s.key!==\"photo\"){ recolor(c); }\n  out[s.key]={id:c.id, type:c.type, w:c.width, h:c.height};\n}\nfunction recolor(node){\n  const targets=[node];\n  ... traverse children: for(const d of node.findAll(()=>true)) plus node itself\n  for(const d of [node,...node.findAll(()=>true)]){\n    if(\"fills\" in d && d.fills && d.fills!==figma.mixed && Array.isArray(d.fills) && d.fills.length){\n      d.fills = d.fills.map(paint=> paint.type===\"SOLID\"? {...paint, color:INK}: paint);\n    }\n    if(\"strokes\" in d && Array.isArray(d.strokes) && d.strokes.length){\n      d.strokes = d.strokes.map(paint=> paint.type===\"SOLID\"? {...paint, color:INK}: paint);\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCareful: function declaration order — define recolor before use (hoisting works for function declarations). OK.\n\nAlso caption labels: add text \"Media (from 04 · Media)\" etc. Minor; skip labels for media, add for others later.\n\nAlso create the section heading text \"Components · Deniz Arslan portfolio system\" at (0,0) 20 Bold ink. And maybe \"01_Work\"/\"02_About\" area labels later.\n\nOutput JSON via console? use_figma returns result of code? The tool returns whatever the code returns/logs? Typically the tool returns the last expression or console output. I'll `return out;`? In plugin sandbox top-level return invalid; assign result = out; and the tool prints? I'll use `console.log(JSON.stringify(out))` — does use_figma capture console? Unknown. Safer: `out` as final expression. Many such tools return the final expression value. I'll end code with `JSON.stringify(out)`.\n\nNow Call B: NavLink + TextLink component sets with hover wiring.\n\n```js\nawait figma.loadFontAsync Regular/Medium/Bold\nconst ws = page 4:2; await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(ws);\nconst C={...};\nconst ACCENT=..., etc.\n\nfunction solid(c,o=1){return {type:\"SOLID\",color:c,opacity:o};}\n\nasync function makeTextLinkVariant(name, {icon, hover}){\n  const comp=figma.createComponent();\n  comp.name=name;\n  comp.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\";\n  comp.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"; comp.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";\n  comp.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";\n  comp.itemSpacing=8;\n  comp.paddingLeft=comp.paddingRight=2; comp.paddingTop=comp.paddingBottom=2;\n  comp.fills=[];\n  const t=figma.createText();\n  t.fontName={family:\"DM Sans\",style:\"Medium\"};\n  t.characters=\"Label\";\n  t.fontSize=16;\n  t.lineHeight={value:24,unit:\"PIXELS\"};\n  t.fills=[solid(hover?C.accent:C.secondary)]; // nav colors differ\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nWait NavLink colors: Default No = secondary #6F6B66; Hover No = accent; Yes = accent both. Underline on hover: t.textDecoration = \"UNDERLINE\".\n\nNavLink variant maker:\n```js\nfunction navVariant(current, hover){\n  const comp=figma.createComponent();\n  comp.name=`Current=${current}, State=${hover?\"Hover\":\"Default\"}`;\n  comp.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\"; sizing AUTO/AUTO;\n  comp.paddingLeft=comp.paddingRight=0; top/bottom=4;\n  comp.fills=[];\n  const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:\"DM Sans\",style:\"Medium\"}; t.characters=\"Work\"; t.fontSize=16; t.lineHeight={value:24,unit:\"PIXELS\"};\n  t.fills=[solid(C.accent)]; // current yes; hover no: accent; default no: secondary\n  if(hover) t.textDecoration=\"UNDERLINE\";\n  ...\n}\n```\nColors: current===\"Yes\" → accent; else hover? accent : secondary.\n\nThen combineAsVariants. Then wire hover: for pairs (Default→Hover, Hover→Default) with same Current. Set reactions on variant masters:\n```js\nvDefault.reactions=[{trigger:{type:\"MouseEnter\"},action:{type:\"CHANGE_TO\",destinationId:vHover.id}}];\nvHover.reactions=[{trigger:{type:\"MouseLeave\"},action:{type:\"CHANGE_TO\",destinationId:vDefault.id}}];\n```\nHmm CHANGE_TO might need \"transition\"? optional.\n\nPosition set: navSet.x=0, y=360; variants inside set are auto-arranged. The ComponentSetNode position: set x,y after combine (combineAsVariants(nodes, parent) returns set; then set.x=...).\n\nTextLink variants: text color always accent; hover underline. Icon: None/Right/UpRight — icon instance from cloned icon masters (need their IDs from Call A — returned via out). I'll capture IDs. Icon instance rescale(16/24). Fill override to accent: find vector child in instance, set fills accent.\n\nInstance inside component master = nested instance; fill override on its child allowed.\n\nTextLink structure: [text, icon (if any)]. itemSpacing 8, counterAlign CENTER. Padding 2 sides for hover click area.\n\nCombine 6 variants → ComponentSet \"Text Link\".\n\nThen Header & Footer (Call C) need NavLink set IDs; and instances of specific variants: variantNode.createInstance().\n\nHeader:\n```js\nconst header=figma.createComponent();\nheader.name=\"Header\";\nheader.layoutMode=\"VERTICAL\"; primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO (hug height), counterAxisSizingMode FIXED (width set 1440);\nheader.resizeWithoutConstraints(1440, 88)? With layout, set counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" then width=1440.\nheader.fills=[];\nRow=figma.createFrame(); Row.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\"; primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" width stretch? Row inside vertical: layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\"; counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\"; primaryAxisAlignItems=\"SPACE_BETWEEN\"; padding 0 80; height: counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\", resize height 88.\nRow.fills=[];\nlogo text \"da.\" 28 Bold ink;\nnav=frame HORIZONTAL gap 40 AUTO sizing; fills=[];\nnav instances: work=navNoDefault.createInstance() text override \"Work\"... wait text is \"Work\" already default. Overrides only needed for About/Playground/Contact: t.characters=\"About\" etc. Instance child text: inst.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\").\nheader children: Row, Line(rect h1 stretch fill divider).\n```\nrect in auto-layout vertical: r=figma.createRectangle(); r.resize(100,1); r.fills=[solid(C.divider)]; r.layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\";\n\nHeader component height: Row 88 + line 1 = 89.\n\nFooter:\n```js\nfooter VERTICAL counterAxis FIXED width 1440, primary AUTO;\nLine rect stretch h1 fill divider;\nRow HORIZONTAL layoutAlign STRETCH padding 28 80 SPACE_BETWEEN counterAlign CENTER fills none;\n left text \"Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020\" 14 Regular secondary lh 20;\n right row gap 40: 3 TextLink instances (Icon=None,Default) text override \"Artstation\"/\"LinkedIn\"/\"Twitter\", fontSize override 14? default 16 — set 14.\n```\nSocial links color: accent (TextLink) — or ink? Accent links everywhere consistent. OK.\n\nCall D: ImagePlaceholder + ProjectBlock variants + SkillList.\n\nImagePlaceholder