lpted in ZBrush, retopologized and UV-mapped in Maya, textured in Mari, rendered with Arnold.\" — instance overrides for P2/P3: tools.visible=false.\n\nImagePlaceholder instance inside block: default 660×440.\n\nFor Status variant, clone Link variant then modify? Easier: build via same builder function twice with flag. Then combineAsVariants([linkComp, statusComp]) → \"Project Block\".\n\nSkillList:\n```js\ncomp \"Skill List\" VERTICAL counterAxis FIXED width 624? Let me hug: counterAxisSizingMode AUTO with title + rows hug... rows text width variable; fixed width 624 better: counterAxis FIXED, resize(624, h). primary AUTO.\nchildren:\n title 12 Medium ls 8% muted uppercase text \"Main Software\" (characters as given: \"Main Software\" — brief uses title case; uppercase transform visual? If I set text uppercase \"MAIN SOFTWARE\" it changes copy. Keep \"Main Software\" as-is, styled small muted.)\n spacer? divider under title: rect h1 stretch fill divider with top margin — use itemSpacing: title, then rows container VERTICAL gap 0: [Row, div, Row, div...]. \n Row: frame HORIZONTAL? just text with padding: row frame VERTICAL? Simply text nodes with padding via wrapper frames? Easier: rows as text nodes with height set? Text in vertical auto-layout with itemSpacing and divider rects between: sequence: title (paddingBottom? no per-child padding; use gaps).\n Structure: SkillList VERTICAL itemSpacing 0, children:\n   title text (with paddingBottom via a wrapper? no) — add itemSpacing 0 and rely on explicit spacer rects? Messy.\n Alternative: SkillList VERTICAL itemSpacing 0:\n   TitleWrap frame VERTICAL padding 0 0 16 0 AUTO sizing, child title text\n   Row1Wrap frame VERTICAL padding 14 0, child text\n   Div rect h1 stretch\n   Row2Wrap ... etc\n 6 rows → children: TitleWrap, Row1, Div, Row2, Div, Row3, Div, Row4, Div, Row5, Div, Row6 = 12 children.\n Row wrap: HORIZONTAL? VERTICAL hug; text stretch.\n```\nFine. Overrides per instance: title characters; row texts.\n\nContactBlock (Call E):\n```js\ncomp VERTICAL gap 36 counterAxis FIXED width 1280? hug? heading width 1000 max. Set counterAxisSizingMode AUTO with heading text width fixed 980 (textAutoResize HEIGHT). Heading row: HORIZONTAL gap 24 counterAlign CENTER: heading text (width 980, HEIGHT auto) + arrow icon instance (accent, rescale 1.5 → 36). Row wraps? heading 40/48: \"I'd be thrilled to hear about your next project\" at 40px ≈ 21 chars/line*? width 980 → likely 2 lines. Icon 36 centered vs 2-line heading (96 tall) → center align.\n Links row: gap 48: email TextLink (fontSize 20), resume TextLink (fontSize 20).\n```\n\nContactBlock name \"Contact Block\".\n\nThen Call F/G build frames; Call H wiring; Call I screenshots.\n\nAlso add labels under masters? Skip to reduce risk; component names suffice (visible in layers panel). Maybe add one heading text \"Components · Deniz Arslan portfolio system\" at (0,0) 20 Bold ink. And maybe \"01_Work\"/\"02_About\" area labels later.\n\nlayoutGrids on page frames:\n```js\nframe.layoutGrids=[{pattern:\"COLUMNS\", sectionSize?...}] — ColumnGrid: {pattern:\"COLUMNS\", count:12, gutterSize? Actually property names: {pattern:\"COLUMNS\", count:12, margin:80, gutter:32? }} LayoutGrid: pattern COLUMNS requires alignment?, gutterSize, count, margin, isVisible. Properties: alignment (\"MIN\"/\"CENTER\"...), gutterSize, count, sectionSize, margin, offset. For COLUMNS: {pattern:\"COLUMNS\", count:12, gutterSize:32, margin:80, alignment:\"MIN\"? } I think margin works when alignment MIN/CENTER. Set {pattern:\"COLUMNS\", count:12, gutterSize:32, margin:80, alignment:\"CENTER\"}? Hmm risk of API complaints. I'll try; wrap in try/catch — non-critical.\n```\n\nOK also: intro para width 620 fixed: create text, set textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\", resize(620, 10) (height auto-adjusts). In auto-layout child with fixed width: layoutAlign \"MIN\" keeps left. Good.\n\nBig headings: width 1280/720 fixed with HEIGHT auto.\n\nNow let me think about fill of page frames: white bg. Root frame fill solid(C.bg).\n\nPage frames also clipsContent default true fine.\n\nLet me write Call A now.\n\nAlso: potential problem — cloning component master 2:5 then instance creation: instances must reference the clone (master in workspace). Fine.\n\nAlso I should double check node 2:5's type/size at runtime and photo content (imagePaint?). Output its fills type maybe. I'll include info in out: for photo: type, w,h, and whether children have image fills.\n\nAlso for icons: their internal vector constraints — for rescale later, rescale() handles scaling regardless.\n\nOne more: the workspace page currently empty; after setCurrentPageAsync, figma.currentPage = ws.\n\nLet me also think about what `combineAsVariants(nodes, parent, index)` returns — ComponentSetNode. Its name defaults to concatenation? Set name manually: \"Nav Link\", \"Text Link\", \"Project Block\".\n\nVariant selection property names come from component names (\"Current=No, State=Default\").\n\nInstance variant override: instance.setProperties({\"Current\":\"Yes\",\"State\":\"Default\"})? Setting subset OK.\n\nAlso CHANGE_TO action needs the variant to belong to same set — yes.\n\nAlright, Call A code. Let me also compute where to put things — final layout:\n\nComponents area:\n- Title text (0,0)\n- Nav Link set (0, 80) — variants each ~120 wide → set ~500×60\n- Text Link set (0, 200) — 6 variants ~180 wide → ~1100×60\n- Header master (0, 320) 1440×89\n- Footer master (0, 460) 1440×~93\n- Image Placeholder (0, 620) 660×440\n- Project Block set (720, 620) — variants 1280 wide each; set arranges grid — 2 variants side by side = 2600 wide?? combineAsVariants default layout horizontal. Set at (720,620) would span to 3320. Fine but wide; or set vertical stacking? ComponentSet layout auto; can I control? The set has its own padding/cursor... There's set.layoutMode? ComponentSetNode doesn't support layoutMode I think (it auto-arranges variants horizontally? Actually variants arrange in