{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The metadata shows only the old nodes — the NavLink/TextLink components are NOT visible. That means the error occurred before creating them? Wait, the error was \"in set_reactions\" — that means the code got to the reactions part. But combineAsVariants happened before... unless the whole call was rolled back on error? Figma plugin execution inside use_figma might run in a transaction that rolls back on error. The metadata shows no new components — so yes, the entire call was rolled back.\n\nOK so I need error-free code. Everything is gone; redo Call B with correct reactions format. Also since nothing persists from failed calls, I'll be careful.\n\nAlso note: reactions assignment threw, so nothing after it executed, and everything rolled back.\n\nLet me redo Call B with corrected trigger/action formats:\n- trigger: {type:\"MOUSE_ENTER\"} / {type:\"MOUSE_LEAVE\"}\n- action: {type:\"NODE\", destinationId: id, navigation:\"CHANGE_TO\", transition: {type:\"INSTANT\"}}\n\nHmm transition \"INSTANT\" — risky. Options per validation error were not listed. Let me think about what Figma's API accepts. From Figma Plugin API docs (ProtocolActionNavigation):\n\n```\ntransition?: Transition\ntype Transition = TransitionProto... \n```\n\nActually, from the published typings (figma.d.ts):\n\n```ts\ntype Transition = \n  { readonly type: 'NO_CONNECTION' } |\n  { readonly type: 'INSTANT' } |   // ??? not sure\n  ...\n```\n\nHmm. I recall in the REST API there are transitions like \"DISSOLVE\", \"SMART_ANIMATE\", \"MOVE_IN\", \"MOVE_OUT\", \"SLIDE_IN\", \"SLIDE_OUT\", \"PUSH\", \"SCROLL_ANIMATE\". And there's also the \"INSTANT\" for prototype default \"None\"? In the UI, transitions include \"Instant\", \"Dissolve\", \"Smart animate\", \"Move in/out\", \"Slide in/out\", \"Push\". So INSTANT likely exists in the API as {type: \"INSTANT\"}.\n\nTo be safe, I'll wrap each reactions assignment in try/catch and use fallback transition {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.1, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}} if INSTANT fails. But wait — does the transition property even need easing for DISSOLVE? DISSOLVE requires duration + easing per typings? They might be optional. I'll include duration and easing to be safe.\n\nActually, simpler: try {type:\"INSTANT\"} first for each; catch → try {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.1, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}; catch → try without transition.\n\nBut errors roll back everything... unless I catch them. If I catch, the state persists. Good — wrap risky calls in try/catch so the whole script never throws.\n\nAlso for the CHANGE_TO navigation: maybe the validation accepts navigation:\"CHANGE_TO\". The error listed for NODE action: \"Required value missing at [0].action.navigation\" — meaning navigation is required, enum includes presumably NAVIGATE/OVERLAY/SWAP/CHANGE_TO/SCROLL_TO. I'll try \"CHANGE_TO\".\n\nAlso for Easing: {type:\"EASE_OUT\"} should be valid.\n\nLet me also reconsider: is hover variant-switching worth the risk? It's nice-to-have. The core requirement is click navigation. I'll implement with try/catch fallbacks so failure won't roll back. If INSTANT fails and DISSOLVE fails, skip hover wiring (log via notify?). I can't read output... I'll just make the code robust.\n\nActually — I could test the transition schema cheaply: try assigning with INSTANT in try/catch; if throws, try DISSOLVE; if throws, try {type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\",duration:0.2,easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}; else skip. Fine.\n\nAdditionally, I realize I should double check: can I set reactions on variant masters for CHANGE_TO? That's the standard way. OK.\n\nAlso — since I can't get return values, I'll rely on get_metadata after each call to discover IDs. To make discovery easy, I'll position components at known coordinates and give distinctive names.\n\nLet me redo Call B fully, with try/catch around everything risky, and verify via metadata afterward.","signature":"213755f373884ce28d3ef