{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a full product design inside Figma file https://www.figma.com/design/4GPvqXGwp8Aaq4DfmSvw0k/ (fileKey `4GPvqXGwp8Aaq4DfmSvw0k`). Explicit instructions:\n   - Read 「00·Start Here」 for the design task, 「01·Foundations」 for visual specs, reuse 「02·Components」, use 「04·Media」 assets, deliver the complete design to 「03·Workspace」.\n   - Must call whoami before writing and confirm account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (DONE — confirmed).\n   - Preserve all reference pages and their nodes; keep unrelated content intact; do not create a different file or switch accounts.\n   - If app name in external query disagrees with brief, use product in 00 · Start Here.\n   - Workflow: whoami → get_metadata → read-only use_figma inspection → use_figma building → get_screenshot verification. Use supplied Figma tools directly, no delegation.\n   - Use valid Plugin API calls; load fonts before text editing; build in manageable sections; check tool results.\n   - Add prototype interactions required by brief after screens exist.\n   - Inspect screenshots of ALL required screens; fix visible problems; screenshot success alone ≠ completion.\n   - Unattended session: resolve routine choices using the brief, don't wait for humans; report real limitations if blocked.\n   - Finish with: assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations.\n   - FORMAT REQUIREMENT: Every assistant message containing a tool call must include a concise decision summary prefixed exactly `Reasoning summary:` in the same message; after each tool result do the same before next call. Final response: `Reasoning summary: ...` on first line, then `Final answer:` and the answer.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma (JS, ≤50000 chars/call)\n   - CRITICAL LESSON 1: use_figma returns \"Code executed with no return value\" — code return values are NOT readable; discover created node IDs via get_metadata afterward\n   - CRITICAL LESSON 2: any uncaught error in use_figma ROLLS BACK the entire call; wrap risky ops (e.g., reactions) in try/catch\n   - Reactions schema (learned from validation error): trigger `{type:\"MOUSE_ENTER\"|\"MOUSE_LEAVE\"|\"ON_CLICK\"|\"MOUSE_LEAVE\"|...}` (NOT \"MouseEnter\"); actions: `{type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"|\"CHANGE_TO\"|\"SCROLL_TO\"|..., transition:...}` (CHANGE_TO is a navigation value, not an action.type; transition appears required — fallback chain: `{type:\"INSTANT\"}` → `{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.1,easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}` → omit)\n   - Auto-layout: layoutMode, primaryAxisSizingMode/counterAxisSizingMode (\"AUTO\"|\"FIXED\"), itemSpacing, layoutAlign:\"STRETCH\", counterAxisAlignItems (\"BASELINE\"|\"CENTER\"|\"MIN\"), primaryAxisAlignItems:\"SPACE_BETWEEN\", textAutoResize:\"HEIGHT\"\n   - Component sets via figma.combineAsVariants; variant naming \"Prop=Value, Prop=Value\"; instance.setProperties({Prop:\"Value\"}); nested instance overrides (text characters, fontSize, visibility, nested variant props)\n   - figma.clone for copying component masters; node.rescale(scale) with resize fallback\n   - Fonts: DM Sans Regular/Medium/Bold loaded via figma.loadFontAsync before any text work\n   - Must use `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)`; never use loadAllPagesAsync/setPluginData/createImageAsync\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file 4GPvqXGwp8Aaq4DfmSvw0k** — only assigned file; pages: 0:1 (brief), 1:2 (foundations), 1:3 (components, empty), 1:4 (media), 4:2 (03 · Workspace — build target, now populated with components)\n   - **Brief content (00 · Start Here, node 3:2)** — fixed data verbatim:\n     - 01_Work must include: Footer \"Deniz Arslan ⏤ 2020\" · Artstation · LinkedIn · Twitter; Header logo \"da.\" · nav Work/About/Playground/Contact · current: Work; Intro \"Hello, I'm Deniz.\" · \"A senior-year design student who is trying to specialize in 3D modeling & texturing.\" · scroll cue (Icon_Arrow_Down); 3 project blocks (number+name, description, tools line where given, link or status, image placeholder)\n     - 02_About must include: Contact \"I'd be thrilled to hear about your next project\" (Icon_Arrow_Right) · \"deniz.arslan@example.com\" · \"View Resume\"; Footer; Header current: About; Intro \"Hi, I'm Deniz Arslan, 3D artist & sculptor.\" · biography (2 paragraphs) · Photo_Profile; Skills \"Main Software\" + \"Main Skills\" lists\n     - LINKS: 01_Work: About(nav)→02_About; logo \"da.\", Work(nav)→01_Work(self). 02_About: logo \"da.\", Work(nav)→01_Work\n     - Projects: 01 / Goblin Bust — desc \"Goblin concept digital sculpture with human-like skin. Learned a lot of quick tips and look development.\" tools \"Sculpted in ZBrush, retopologized and UV-mapped in Maya, textured in Mari, rendered with Arnold.\" link \"More shots from this project ↗\"; 02 / Skin Shader Study — \"Subsurface weight, specular roughness and diffuse maps generated with procedural and manual techniques.\" link \"See case study →\"; 03 / Creature Concept — \"Experimental creature modeling for a school project.\" status \"Project WIP\" (not a link)\n     - Biography P1: \"My work is mainly focused on 3D modeling, texturing and rendering. I like exploring creatures with a touch of dark surrealism for characters and production.\" P2: \"Now I'm an interactive media design student in Istanbul ⏤ currently freelancing and seeking internship opportunities.\"\n     - Skills: Main Software: Pixologic ZBrush, Autodesk Maya, The Foundry Mari, Arnold Renderer, Blender, Forger · Adobe CC, Figma, Ableton; Main Skills: Organic and Polygonal Modeling, UV Layout, Texturing, Retopology, Illustration, Sound Design\n     - Entry-only (no frames): Playground, Contact, project links, socials, email, View Resume\n   - **Foundations**: brand ink #181717, accent blue #2429AF, DM Sans, 1440 desktop, light mode\n   - **My design system** (self-defined): secondary #6F6B66 {111,107,102}, muted #98938C {152,147,140}, divider #E7E4E0 {231,228,224}, placeholder #EDEAE6 {237,234,230}, subtle #F6F4F1 {246,244,241}, ghost number #DDD9D4 {221,217,212}, bg white; type: logo 28 Bold, display 64/72 Bold, hero 56/64, section 40 Medium, project name 26/34 Medium, body 16/26, small 14/22, label 12 Medium ls8%; margins 80, content 1280\n   - **Key helper functions used in every call**:\n     ```js\n     function solid(c,o=1){return {type:\"SOLID\",color:c,opacity:o};}\n     function mkText(chars,size,style,color,opts={}){\n       const t=figma.createText();\n       t.fontName={family:\"DM Sans\",style};\n       t.characters=chars;\n       t.fontSize=size;\n       t.lineHeight={value:opts.lh||Math.round(size*1.5),unit:\"PIXELS\"};\n       if(opts.ls!==undefined) t.letterSpacing={value:opts.ls,unit:\"PERCENT\"};\n       if(opts.name) t.name=opts.name;\n       t.fills=[solid(color)];\n       return t;\n     }\n     ```\n   - **Node IDs created in 03 · Workspace (page 4:2)**:\n     - Media clones: Photo_Profile master **5:2** (228×320), Icon_Arrow_Down **5:3**, Icon_Arrow_Right **5:5**, Icon_Arrow_Up_Right **5:7** (icons recolored to ink); section title text 5:9\n     - Nav Link set **7:10**: 7:2 Current=No,State=Default; 7:4 No,Hover; 7:6 Yes,Default; 7:8 Yes,Hover (text child named \"Label\"; hover wired MOUSE_ENTER/LEAVE + CHANGE_TO with fallbacks)\n     - Text Link set **7:31**: 7:11 Icon=None,Default; 7:13 None,Hover; 7:15 ArrowRight,Default; 7:19 ArrowRight,Hover; 7:23 ArrowUpRight,Default; 7:27 ArrowUpRight,Hover (children: \"Label\" text + \"Icon\" 16px accent)\n     - Header **8:6** (1440×89): Bar (SPACE