child's COUNTER axis = height??\n\nHold on. layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\" on a child stretches the child along the PARENT's counter axis. Parent is VERTICAL → parent counter axis = horizontal → stretch makes child fill parent's content WIDTH. So child width = 1440 via STRETCH. But child.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\" (hug width) CONFLICTS with stretch. Which wins? Apparently hug won (160?? why 160...). Hmm, actually maybe when both set, Figma... the child re-hugs after children change. Left collapsed to 1 (grow with hug parent = no effect → keeps width... 1?!).\n\nThe cleanest fix: set hero.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" and hero counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\" (height hugs), plus layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\" for width; or simply resize hero to (1440, height). Same for Lists row: row.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" + resize(1280, 365), and instances keep layoutGrow=1 → each 624.\n\nFor hero: resize(1440, hero.height) with primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\". Left already layoutGrow=1 → gets 1280-80-399=801.\n\nAlso Left width 1: after hero fixed at 1440, grow gives 801. Its children (title 640 etc.) will fit.\n\nAlso check: photo x=161 — after fix, photo should be at x=80+801+80=961.\n\nSkill instances: with row FIXED 1280 and grow 1 each: (1280-32)/2 = 624 ✓.\n\nAdditionally — I notice Contact Block instance is 1024 wide at x=80 — fine (left-aligned in 1280 content).\n\nAlso the header in About page: nav About current — will verify in screenshot.\n\nAlso 01_Work looks correct now.\n\nLet me also read the __debug text (14:150) — metadata doesn't show characters. I need get_design_context or read via another method to see the reactions JSON. Hmm, metadata shows only name/size/position. The debug text content isn't visible. get_design_context would show text content but it's heavy. Alternatively, keep it simple: after fixing hero/lists, take screenshots; for reactions verification, do the reverse — create debug text per wire result and use get_design_context on just that node? get_design_context on the debug text node would return its characters! That's cheap since it's one text node.\n\nPlan:\n1. use_figma: fix hero (12:96) primaryAxisSizingMode FIXED + resize 1440; fix Lists (12:105) primaryAxisSizingMode FIXED + resize (1280,365); ensure Left layoutGrow=1; update __debug text (14:150) with reactions JSON (rewriting characters — it's already a text node; set characters). Keep node.\n2. get_design_context on 14:150 to read reactions + confirm.\n3. get_screenshot both frames.\n\nActually combining: in the same call as fixes, rewrite debug characters to include reactions info. Then get_design_context(14:150) reads it. Then delete debug node later (before final screenshots? it's at x=3400 y=0 — outside frames, but I'll delete it at the end for cleanliness).","signature":"5391650562ca488b9bb8b76e"}],"id":"77dad873-96cf-4b1a-bff1-bb3a0f27b557","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89a64135-6412-4ef4-999c-ac66165ec06a","uuid":"6834e6cf-b4e0-43e5-9c79-b80e6b5727a6","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:47:45.640Z","thinking_duration_ms":53721}
