ON_CLICK → NODE dest, navigation NAVIGATE, transition INSTANT.\n\nHotspots needed on 01_Work:\n1. Over \"Nav/About\" instance → dest 12:81\n2. Over \"Nav/Work\" instance → dest 11:21 (self)\n3. Over logo text → dest 11:21\n4. Scroll cue (11:39) — it's a regular instance child of intro frame (11:36 auto-layout). Wait — 11:39 is an instance of Icon_Arrow_Down component (5:3). Reactions on an INSTANCE (top-level instance, not child of instance) — is that supported? The nav items are instances too but they're children of the Header INSTANCE. The scroll cue is an instance whose parent is a plain frame (intro). Setting reactions on a top-level instance should work (instances support interactions overrides). But it also failed? cue reactions [] — cue is instance child of plain frame. Hmm, so even top-level instance reactions failed?!\n\nWait — all tested nodes were instances (nav items are instances inside header instance; logo is a TEXT child of header instance; cue is an instance child of intro frame). All came back []. So reactions can't be set on instance children (logo, nav items) — expected — AND apparently not on cue (top-level instance) either?? That's surprising. Unless... the wire() caught errors and all 3 variants failed.\n\nHmm, actually wait: maybe reactions DID fail to be read back? I read `n.reactions` right after — they were set in a PREVIOUS call (Call H). In this call I only READ them. Maybe reactions set in previous call were persisted... they're empty. Or maybe reactions can't be READ from instance children (returns [])? Possibly reading instance children reactions returns the main component's reactions (which are empty) — overrides might exist but not visible via API?\n\nRegardless — the reliable path: hotspots as regular rectangles (not instances). For the scroll cue: instead of relying on instance reactions, place a hotspot rect over it too (in intro frame, ABSOLUTE).\n\nHmm wait — but actually there's another approach for nav items that avoids hotsp