{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Very informative! The reactions setter throws validation errors on ALL tested nodes (navMaster \"err set\", cueSet \"err set\", navChildSet \"err set\", rectSet \"err set\"). The error message reveals the expected schema:\n\nKey parts from the error:\n- \"Expected [O]action to be one of the following, but none matched: [O]action|conditionalBlock\" — action must have `type` as one of recognized values.\n- It lists: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' | 'NODE' | 'URL' | ... for [O]action.type\" — recognized: BACK, CLOSE, NODE, URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME, SET_VARIABLE...\n- For action.type NODE: \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" — WAIT, that says for the NODE action, keys destinationId/navigation/transition are NOT recognized?!\n\nHmm wait, let me re-read: \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition' at [O]action|urn\" — hmm \"[O]action|urn\" — the URN action? The error lists problems for each possible action variant. For the variant where type=\"URL\", the expected key is \"url\" — extra keys destinationId/navigation/transition unrecognized THERE. That's the mismatch report for the URL variant, not NODE.\n\n- \"Invalid literal value, expected 'UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME' ... \" for another variant.\n- \"Expected 'transition' to be one of the following, but none matched\" — and lists: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'DISSOLVE' | 'SMART_ANIMATE' | 'SCROLL_ANIMATE' | ... received 'INSTANT'\" — THERE IT IS! transition type \"INSTANT\" is NOT a valid enum! Valid: DISSOLVE, SMART_ANIMATE, SCROLL_ANIMATE, MOVE_IN, MOVE_OUT, PUSH, SLIDE_IN, SLIDE_OUT. For instant navigation there's... hmm \"SCROLL_ANIMATE\"? Also \"Required value missing at [O]action.transition.direction\" — for MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT, \"direction\" is required. For DISSOLVE: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'DISSOLVE' | 'SMART_ANIMATE' | 'SCROLL_ANIMATE', received 'INSTANT'\" — so transition must be DISSOLVE/SMART_ANIMATE/SCROLL_ANIMATE with {duration, easing}, or MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT with {direction, duration?, easing?}.\n\n- Also \"Required value missing at [O]action.transition.matchLayers\", \"Required value missing at [O]action.transition.duration\", \"Required value missing at [O]action.transition.easing\" — so transition requires duration, easing (and matchLayers for SMART_ANIMATE?).\n\n- Also: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'INSTANT' | 'MOVE_IN'...\" hmm there's \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'INSTANT' | 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'INSTANT'\" — confusing. And \"'navigation' | 'transition'\" keys... \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'navigation', 'transition' at [O]action|destinationId\" — so for the NODE action variant, the recognized key is `destinationId` ONLY?? \"Expected 'node' ... 'nodeId'\"? Hmm: \"Invalid literal value, expected 'NODE'...\" \n\nLet me parse more carefully from visible text:\n\nLine snippets:\n1. `\"navMaster\": \"err set\", \"cueSet\": \"err set\", \"rectSet\": \"err set\"` — wait rectSet also \"err set\"! Even a plain rectangle failed?? Hmm: `\"rectSet\":\"err set\",\"rectRead\":\"[]\"}` at the end. And `\"navChildSet\":\"err set\",\"navChildRead\":\"[]\"`.\n\nSo ALL failed with validation error. The schema for reactions in THIS Figma API version differs from what I used. The error text (from zod) says:\n\n- \"Property 'reactions' failed validation: Expected [O]action to be one of the following, but none matched: [O]action|conditionalBlock | [O]action|type ... Required value missing at [O]action|conditionalBlock@s | Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'type'\"\n\nHmm interesting — \"[O]action|conditionalBlock ... Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'type'\" — maybe the first union member is a conditional block with key \"s\"? Confusing.\n\n- \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' | 'NODE' | 'URL' | ... received ...\" — hmm this is about action.type? It says \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'type'\" somewhere — weird.\n\n- \"at [O]action|urn ... Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" — the URN action variant (type URL?) expects key... \n\n- \"Invalid literal value, expected 'UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME' at [O]action|type ... Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'mediaAction'\" \n\n- \"Required value missing at [O]action|mediaAction|@toJsonIp\" ...\n\n- \"Invalid literal value, expected 'SET_VARIABLE' at [O]action|type ... Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'variableId', 'variableMode'...\" \"Expected 'SET_VARIABLE_MODE' | 'SET_VARIABLE'\"...\n\n- \"Invalid literal value, expected 'condition'...\" — conditional actions.\n\n- \"Expected 'transition' to be one of the following, but none matched: ... Invalid enum value. Expected 'DISSOLVE' | 'SMART_ANIMATE' | 'SCROLL_ANIMATE', received 'INSTANT'\" — CRITICAL: transition.type INSTANT invalid. Options include DISSOLVE, SMART_ANIMATE, SCROLL_ANIMATE, and directional: MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT (each requires 'direction').\n\n- \"Required value missing at [O]action|transition|duration\" — duration REQUIRED for DISSOLVE etc.\n- \"Required value missing at [O]action|transition|easing\" — easing REQUIRED.\n- \"Required value missing at [O]action|transition|matchLayers\" — for SMART_ANIMATE.\n- \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'LEFT' | 'RIGHT' | 'TOP' | 'BOTTOM'\" presumably for direction.\n- \"Required value missing at [O]action|transition|direction\" — direction required for MOVE_*/PUSH/SLIDE_*.\n\nAnd about the action NODE shape: \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'navigation', 'transition' at [O]action|destinationId\" — hmm, this suggests the NODE action variant is keyed by... Actually maybe the union member for NODE is identified via \"destinationId\" only, and 'navigation'/'transition' are NOT allowed on NODE action?? That contradicts the plugin API docs where NavigationAction = {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation, transition}. \n\nHmm wait — maybe this Figma MCP \"use_figma\" runs a NEWER plugin API where reactions schema changed to the \"prototype via variables/conditions\" format? The listed types: BACK, CLOSE, NODE, URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME, SET_VARIABLE (mode?), CONDITIONAL... and for NODE: \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'navigation', 'transition'\" — no wait...\n\nLook again: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' | 'NODE' | 'URL' | ... received\" — probably from \"[O]action|type\" with expected BACK|CLOSE|NODE|URL|UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME|SET_VARIABLE|SET_VARIABLE_MODE|CONDITIONAL.\n\nThen for the NODE member: \"Invalid literal value, expected 'NODE'\" would appear if type matched partially... And \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" — hmm, maybe for the member where type='URL', expected key 'url', and destinationId/navigation/transition are unrecognized. Similarly for member type='BACK'/'CLOSE' — no keys allowed. The zod error reports ALL union members' failures. So the ones mentioning \"destinationId... unrecognized\" are just the non-NODE members. The NODE member's specific failure might be the transition: since transition INSTANT invalid → whole union failed.\n\nSo the actionable fix: use transition {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.2/0.3, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}} — with duration AND easing required. But wait — earlier (Call B) the wire() fallback chain tried INSTANT first, then DISSOLVE with duration 0.1 + easing EASE_OUT, then no transition. All variants threw? navMaster read = \"err set\" — and navMaster reactions were set in Call B... but navMaster.reactions now read as... the debug shows `\"navMaster\":\"err set\"` — hmm no wait, navMaster in THIS diagnostic was reading `JSON.stringify(m.reactions)` — it shows \"err set\"?? That means m.reactions STRINGIFIED to the string \"err set\"?? No — look: `out.navMaster=JSON.stringify(m.reactions);` then `out.navMaster` = the stringified reactions. The debug text shows `\"navMaster\": \"[{...MOUSE_ENTER...}]\"`? The first line reads: `\"navMaster\":\"[{\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"MOUSE_ENTER\\\"},...` — actually first chars: `\"navMaster\": \"[{\"trigger\":...` Hmm the screenshot first line: `\"navMaster\":\"[{...trigger...MOUSE_ENTER...` \n\nWait the very beginning: `{\"navMaster\": \"[{...` — I see `{\"navMaster\": \"[{...` hmm actually it reads `\"navMaster\": \"[{s\"trigger\"...`. The rest of line 1: `...\"cueSet\":\"err set\", \"rectSet\":...` no...\n\nLine 1 from screenshot: `{\"navMaster\": \"[{...` — hard to read. It shows: `\"navMaster\":\"[{\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"MOUSE_ENTER\\\"},\\\"action\\\":...` then `\"cueSet\":\"err set\"...` Hmm, the visible text: line 1 ends with `\"navMaster\":\"[{\"trigger\":{\"type\":\"MOUSE_ENTER\"},\"action\":...` I can see \"MOUSE_ENTER\" at the start. Then `\"cueSet\":\"err set\",\"rectSet\":...` — the first visible line: `{\"navMaster\": \"[{\"trigger\":...` then later `...\"cueSet\":\"err set\"` appears mid-line-1. OK so:\n\n- navMaster: reactions successfully contain MOUSE_ENTER wiring → Call B component hover wiring WORKED and persisted! (It used... wait, how did Call B succeed if INSTANT transition invalid? In Call B my fallback chain: INSTANT → DISSOLVE → omit transition. The 2nd variant DISSOLVE duration 0.1 EASE_OUT must have succeeded for the masters. But now in the diagnostic, cueSet/navChildSet/rectSet all \"err set\" — because my diagnostic used ONLY the INSTANT variant which is invalid. Right! The diagnostic only tried ONE variant with INSTANT → all \"err set\". And the earlier Call H wire() had the 3-variant chain — for those, variant 1 (INSTANT) fails, variant 2 (DISSOLVE 0.2 EASE_OUT)... should have succeeded! But Call H reads showed empty reactions...\n\nHmm wait, why did Call H wiring end up empty then? In the diagnostic earlier (before this one), I read reactions of aboutNav1/workNav1/logo1/cue/workNav2/logo2 — all []. But wire() in Call H should have fallen back to DISSOLVE variant and succeeded like in Call B.\n\nUnless... in Call H, wire() DID succeed with DISSOLVE variant, but READING reactions on instance children returns [] (reads don't reflect overrides on instance children). And cue (top-level instance)? Read also []. Hmm.\n\nBut navMaster (component master 7:2) read shows MOUSE_ENTER reactions — masters read fine.\n\nSo current state is AMBIGUOUS for instances: either (a) wiring failed silently despite fallback, or (b) wiring succeeded but reads on instances return underlying component reactions.\n\nKey difference between Call B (masters, succeeded with DISSOLVE variant) and Call H (instance children): in Call B the setter was on component masters. In Call H, setters were on instance children + top-level instance. The most likely truth: setting reactions on instance CHILDREN throws (not supported) — all 3 variants failed → wire() recorded \"ALL FAILED\" in errors (unread). For cue (top-level instance) — maybe also throws? \"Cannot set reactions on an instance\"? Actually top-level instances DO support interaction overrides in the UI... but via API maybe `reactions` on instance is read-only (mirror of master)? \n\nAnd navChildRead returned [] — consistent with not settable.\n\nNew approach — hotspots (plain rectangles) definitely CAN hold reactions? rectSet was \"err set\" BUT the diagnostic rect used INSTANT transition → validation error. With DISSOLVE+duration+easing it should work (as proven by navMaster success in Call B).\n\nAlso — what about nav hover states? They live on component masters (Call B, MOUSE_ENTER↔CHANGE_TO variant). Those are persisted (navMaster read shows reactions). But wait — MOUSE_ENTER with CHANGE_TO... in Call B the action was {type:\"NODE\", destinationId:7:4, navigation:\"CHANGE_TO\", transition:DISSOLVE...}. And it persisted. \n\nSo the plan now:\n1. Hotspot rectangles (plain, fills=[]) over: logo, nav items, scroll cue — in each page frame. Reactions: ON_CLICK, action {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.3, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}}. Hmm — DISSOLVE transition on NAVIGATE gives a fade. Fine. Or omit transition? \"Required value missing at transition\" — for the NODE action variant, transition might be optional in UI but zod said \"Required value missing\"? The messages \"Required value missing at [O]action|transition|duration\" — that's within transition object. Was transition itself required? There was \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" for URL member etc. Can't tell if transition optional for NODE. Keep DISSOLVE 0.3 EASE_OUT (known-good shape from Call B).\n\nActually for NAVIGATE, real Figma default transition is \"Instant\" — but API rejects INSTANT. DISSOLVE 0.3 is acceptable (fade). Hmm wait — is there \"SMART_ANIMATE\"? needs matchLayers. SCROLL_ANIMATE for scroll interactions. For SCROLL_TO action... \"SCROLL_TO\" navigation value with transition SCROLL_ANIMATE? In UI, \"Scroll to\" has its own animation options. I'll use SCROLL_TO + transition DISSOLVE? Odd. Try SCROLL_TO with {type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3,easing:EASE_OUT} fallback to no-transition, fallback to SCROLL_ANIMATE.\n\nHmm, wait — what about navigation value? For NODE action: navigation \"NAVIGATE\" | \"SCROLL_TO\" | \"CHANGE_TO\" | \"SWAP\"... The error listed somewhere \"Invalid enum value. Expected ... 'NAVIGATE'...\"? I saw \"received 'INSTANT'\" multiple times for transition. For navigation I didn't see an error line explicitly... there was \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" repeated for other members. OK.\n\n2. For hover-vs-hotspot conflict: hotspot sits ON TOP of nav items → may swallow hover. Mitigation: make hotspots only cover the nav TEXT area but the hover variant switch happens on the Nav Link instance... both overlap. Risk: hover states never trigger in prototype.\n\nAlternative: DON'T put hotspots over nav; instead put the ON_CLICK on the Nav Link COMPONENT variants with destination decided... no, destinations differ per instance.\n\nAlternative: Figma supports interaction overrides on instances via UI. API may support `instance.setReactions`? No such method... Hmm, actually there IS: for instances, you can override interactions using... I recall the Plugin API added support: \"node.reactions\" is settable on InstanceNode children? There's `figma.ungroup`... no.\n\nLet me just empirically test: set cue.reactions with DISSOLVE variant and read back. And set a nav child's reactions with DISSOLVE and read back. If instance-child setting works with valid transition (the earlier [] read may have been because ALL variants failed — wait no, variant 2 DISSOLVE should have worked if settable... unless DISSOLVE in Call H failed for a different reason: duration:0.2, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"} — navMaster in Call B used duration 0.1? I recorded fallback chain INSTANT → DISSOLVE 0.1 EASE_OUT → no transition. And it succeeded on masters).\n\nHmm wait — maybe in Call H the DISSOLVE variant DID succeed on the instances, and reading `.reactions` on instance children just returns the master's reactions ([]). For the cue: top-level instance — read returned [] too. If set succeeded, read should show override? For top-level instances, `reactions` getter — does it reflect overrides? Unclear!\n\nDECISIVE TEST: set cue.reactions (DISSOLVE variant) and read back immediately in same call. If read shows the DISSOLVE reaction → setting+reading works on top-level instances; then the Call H wires on instance children — retest similarly with immediate read. If read empty after successful set (no throw) → overrides exist but invisible to reads; verify via UI? Can't. Then rely on... hmm.\n\nActually — better idea to sidestep ambiguity: put ON_CLICK interactions on the COMPONENT MASTERS of Nav Link (4 variants) with a PLACEHOLDER destination, then per-instance override... no,