The Header COMPONENT master 8:6 contains the \"Logo\" text. What if I set reactions on the Logo TEXT INSIDE THE COMPONENT MASTER (8:6) with dest... master is at page root → set-time rejection (rect test). Hmm, BUT what if I first MOVE the Header master inside a frame? Components inside frames... moving a COMPONENT node into a frame — allowed (component containers). Then set reaction on its Logo child → dest 11:21: is 11:21 an ancestor of the master? NO (master would be in a different container). Non-ancestor → allowed?? THEN move the master back to page root — reactions persist! And ALL INSTANCES inherit: logo click → 01_Work from EVERY instance — which is EXACTLY what the brief wants (logo → 01_Work on both pages)!! \n\n   Wait even better — same trick for the \"Work\" nav: master variant 7:2/7:4 (Current=No) with ON_CLICK → 11:21 would apply to Work nav instances... BUT ALSO to Playground/Contact navs (they're Current=No too) — wrong. UNLESS I distinguish: hmm, the Nav Link component doesn't know which link it is. So no.\n\n   So plan for logo: \n   1. Move Header master 8:6 into 11:21 temporarily? Hmm wait — simpler: the rejection is only for ANCESTOR destinations relative to the NODE carrying the reaction. The Logo text inside master 8:6 (at page root): dest 11:21 — 11:21 does NOT contain 8:6. But the RECT TEST showed page-root nodes get reactions REJECTED entirely (\"destination 12:81 was rejected — destination node may not exist\" — for a rect at page root!). Hmm — that rect test error said DESTINATION rejected, not the rect. So maybe page-root nodes CAN'T have interactions, OR the destination validation is relative to something weird for page-root nodes.\n\n   Ugh, too many unknowns. JUST TEST: create a rect inside 12:81, set reaction dest 11:21 (should work — like workNav2), then move it into 11:21, read back. If persists → done for logo1: delete that rect, instead apply move-trick properly:\n   \n   For logo1: create rect in 12:81 with reaction dest 11:21 →