{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a full product design inside Figma file https://www.figma.com/design/4GPvqXGwp8Aaq4DfmSvw0k/ (fileKey `4GPvqXGwp8Aaq4DfmSvw0k`). Original user message (Chinese): “请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计： Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/4GPvqXGwp8Aaq4DfmSvw0k/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。” Benchmark constraints: call whoami before writing and confirm account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (DONE, confirmed); preserve all reference pages (00/01/02/04) and their nodes; build only in 03 · Workspace (page 4:2); do not create a different file or switch accounts; workflow whoami → get_metadata → read-only use_figma inspection → use_figma build → get_screenshot verify; use valid Plugin API calls, load fonts before text editing; build in manageable sections; add prototype interactions required by brief after screens exist; inspect screenshots of ALL required screens and fix visible problems; unattended session (resolve routine choices per brief); finish with assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations. FORMAT: every message with a tool call must include a summary prefixed exactly `Reasoning summary:`; final response starts with `Reasoning summary: ...` then `Final answer:`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma (JS ≤50000 chars/call)\n   - use_figma NEVER returns values (\"Code executed with no return value\") — verification via get_metadata + a debug text node (14:150) read back via get_screenshot of the node (get_design_context is NOT in the available toolset; get_screenshot of a text node shows its characters)\n   - get_screenshot can time out at 120s (“Figma 远端 get_screenshot 在 120 秒内没有响应，本次调用已中止，可以直接重试”) — safe to retry\n   - Uncaught errors in use_figma ROLL BACK the entire call — wrap risky ops in try/catch\n   - CRITICAL reactions schema (this API version): reaction = `{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, actions:[...]}` — `actions` PLURAL array, NOT singular `action`; NODE action = `{type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"|\"SCROLL_TO\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3,easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}}`; transition is REQUIRED for NODE actions; transition.type \"INSTANT\" is INVALID (valid: DISSOLVE/SMART_ANIMATE/SCROLL_ANIMATE needing duration+easing(+matchLayers for SMART_ANIMATE), or MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT needing direction); triggers are uppercase enums (ON_CLICK, MOUSE_ENTER, MOUSE_LEAVE)\n   - Destination rules: must be a TOP-LEVEL frame (child frames 11:41, instances 11:42 rejected); must NOT be an ancestor of the interaction node (self-frame links impossible directly); page-root nodes cannot carry interactions; instance children CAN carry reaction overrides with correct schema; readback shows both migrated `action` and `actions` fields\n   - Workaround for self-destination (“move-trick”): create node with reaction inside a NON-ancestor frame (set-time validation passes), then reparent into target frame (reactions persist through moves — verification pending)\n   - Auto-layout pitfalls: HORIZONTAL row with primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\" hugs width (collapses children with layoutGrow); fix with primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" + layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\" + resize(1440/1280, h); frames created via createFrame start at 100×100 and MUST be resized\n   - Fonts: DM Sans Regular/Medium/Bold loaded via figma.loadFontAsync before any text edit\n   - Must use `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)`; never use loadAllPagesAsync/setPluginData/createImageAsync\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file 4GPvqXGwp8Aaq4DfmSvw0k** — pages: 0:1 (00 · Start Here brief), 1:2 (01 · Foundations), 1:3 (02 · Components), 1:4 (04 · Media), 4:2 (03 · Workspace — build target)\n   - **Design tokens**: ink #181717 {24,23,23}/255, accent #2429AF {36,41,175}/255, secondary #6F6B66, muted #98938C, divider #E7E4E0, placeholder #EDEAE6, subtle #F6F4F1, white bg; type: logo 28 Bold, display 64/72 Bold, hero 56/64 Bold, section 40 Medium, project name 26/34 Medium, body 16/26, small 14/22, label 12 Medium ls8%\n   - **Standard helper code used in every call**:\n     ```js\n     const ws = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"4:2\");\n     await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(ws);\n     for(const s of [\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"Bold\"]) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"DM Sans\",style:s});\n     function solid(c,o=1){return {type:\"SOLID\",color:c,opacity:o};}\n     function mkText(chars,size,style,color,opts={}){\n       const t=figma.createText();\n       t.fontName={family:\"DM Sans\",style};\n       t.characters=chars;\n       t.fontSize=size;\n       t.lineHeight={value:opts.lh||Math.round(size*1.5),unit:\"PIXELS\"};\n       if(opts.ls!==undefined) t.letterSpacing={value:opts.ls,unit:\"PERCENT\"};\n       if(opts.name) t.name=opts.name;\n       t.fills=[solid(color)];\n       return t;\n     }\n     ```\n   - **Component layer on page 4:2** (all verified): title text 5:9; Photo_Profile 5:2 (228×320); Icon_Arrow_Down 5:3, Icon_Arrow_Right 5:5, Icon_Arrow_Up_Right 5:7 (24px, ink); Nav Link set 7:10 (variants 7:2 Current=No/Default, 7:4 No/Hover, 7:6 Yes/Default, 7:8 Yes/Hover — hover MOUSE_ENTER/LEAVE wiring persisted, text child named \"Label\"); Text Link set 7:31 (7:11 Icon=None/Default, 7:13 None/Hover, 7:15 ArrowRight/Default, 7:19 ArrowRight/Hover, 7:23 ArrowUpRight/Default, 7:27 ArrowUpRight/Hover — children \"Label\" text + \"Icon\"); Header 8:6 (1440×89, children: \"Logo\" text + nav instances \"Nav/Work\",\"Nav/About\",\"Nav/Playground\",\"Nav/Contact\"); Footer 8:19 (1440×94, \"Copy\" + \"Link/Artstation\",\"Link/LinkedIn\",\"Link/Twitter\"); Image Placeholder 9:13 (660×440); Skill List 9:15 (624×365, children \"TitleWrap\">\"Title\", Row1–Row6 each with \"Item\" text); Project Block set 9:61 (CTA=Link 9:35: \"Content\" col with Title row \"Number\"/\"Slash\"/\"Name\", \"Description\", \"Tools\", \"CTA\" Text Link instance + \"Image\" placeholder instance; CTA=Status 9:49 with badge instead); Contact Block 10:18 (1024×168: heading \"I'd be thrilled to hear about your next project\" 40/48 Medium + Icon_Arrow_Right instance rescale 1.5 recolored accent + links row with email/View Resume Text Link instances fontSize 20); System board 10:28 (1240×764: color swatches + type scale + grid note)\n   - **Frame 01_Work (11:21)** at (0,3600), 1440×2393, VERTICAL, white fill, layoutGrids 12-col/32 gutter/80 margin (accent 4%): Header instance 11:22 (Nav/Work set Current=Yes); Intro 11:36 (padding 96/80/112, gap 32: Display 11:37 \"Hello, I'm Deniz.\" 64/72 Bold; Lead 11:38 20/30 secondary width 620; Scroll cue instance 11:39); Projects 11:41 (padding 0/80/140, gap 80): Project 01 = 11:42 (9:35 instance: Number \"01\", Name \"Goblin Bust\", desc \"Goblin concept digital sculpture with human-like skin. Learned a lot of quick tips and look development.\", Tools \"Sculpted in ZBrush, retopologized and UV-mapped in Maya, textured in Mari, rendered with Arnold.\", CTA Label \"More shots from this project\"); Divider 11:56; Project 02 = 11:57 (Number \"02\", Name \"Skin Shader Study\", desc \"Subsurface weight, specular roughness and diffuse maps generated with procedural and manual techniques.\", Tools visible=false, CTA setProperties({Icon:\"ArrowRight\"}) + \"See case study\"); Divider 11:74; Project 03 = 11:75 (9:49 instance: Number \"03\", Name \"Creature Concept\", desc \"Experimental creature modeling for a school project.\", Tools visible=false, badge \"Project WIP\"); Footer 11:87\n   - **Frame 02_About (12:81)** at (1640,3600), 1440×1785: Header instance 12:82 (Nav/About Current=Yes); Hero 12:96 (1440×752, FIXED+STRETCH, padding 96/80, gap 80, counterAxis MIN): Left 12:97 (layoutGrow=1, 801 wide; Display 12:98 \"Hi, I'm Deniz Arslan, 3D artist & sculptor.\" 56/64 Bold width 640; Biography 12:99 with Body 12:100 \"My work is mainly focused on 3D modeling, texturing and rendering. I like exploring creatures with a touch of dark surrealism for characters and production.\" and Body 12:101 \"Now I'm an interactive media design student in Istanbul ⏤ currently freelancing and seeking internship opportunities.\" 16/26 secondary width 560); Photo 12:102 (5:2 instance rescale 1.75 → 399×560); Skills 12:103 (Divider 12:104 1280-wide; Lists 12:105 1280×365 FIXED+STRETCH, gap 32: Skill List/Software 12:106 + Skill List/Skills 12:126 both layoutGrow=1 → 624 each, second has Title \"Main Skills\" + items \"Organic and Polygonal Modeling\",\"UV Layout\",\"Texturing\",\"Retopology\",\"Illustration\",\"Sound Design\"); Contact Section 12:146 (padding 0/80/140) with Contact Block instance 12:147; Footer 12:157\n   - **Debug node 14:150** \"__debug\" at (3400,0) on page 4:2, 760 wide wrapped, fontSize 14 — used to read back JSON results via get_screenshot; MUST BE DELETED before finishing\n   - **Hotspot / Logo rect** (ID not yet known): created inside 12:81 with reaction ON_CLICK→NAVIGATE 11:21 DISSOLVE 0.3 EASE_OUT, then moved into 11:21 with layoutPositioning=\"ABSOLUTE\", positioned over Logo text via absoluteBoundingBox minus frame origin, padded 8px — verification pending\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Frames created at default 100px width**: 01_Work/02_About were VERTICAL frames with counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" but never resized → STRETCH children collapsed (dividers 1px, Hero 160, Left 1, skill instances 34). Fix: `frame.resize(1440, frame.height)` on both — 01_Work fully fixed; dividers became 1280 wide.\n   - **HORIZONTAL rows hugging width**: Hero 12:96 and Lists 12:105 had primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\" (for HORIZONTAL layout primary axis = width) → hug collapsed despite layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\". Fix: set primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" + layoutAlign=\"STRETCH\" + resize(1440/1280, h). Verified: hero 1440×752, row 1280×365, left 801.\n   - **Reactions silently not applying**: initial wiring used singular `action` field + INSTANT transition; all reads came back []. Three-step diagnosis: (a) zod dump showed transition.type \"INSTANT\" invalid enum (valid: DISSOLVE/SMART_ANIMATE/SCROLL_ANIMATE/MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT; duration/easing required; direction required for directional types); (b) with DISSOLVE 0.3 EASE_OUT the error became \"Please update the 'actions' field instead of the 'action' field!\"; (c) with plural `actions` — instance children set OK.\n   - **Destination restrictions** (all empirically confirmed): SCROLL_TO instance 11:42 rejected; child frame 11:41 rejected (\"destination node may not exist\"); ancestor/self-frame 11:21 rejected from nodes inside it (both NAVIGATE and SCROLL_TO); omitting transition fails validation (\"Expected [O].actions[O] to be one of the following, but none matched\"); page-root nodes rejected. Fixes applied: workNav2/logo2/aboutNav1 wired successfully with `actions` + DISSOLVE; logo self-link on 01_Work done via move-trick (created in 12:81, set reaction, moved into 11:21 over logo); Work nav self-link on 01_Work intentionally left click-unwired (ancestor impossible; hover states preserved — documented limitation); scroll cue left unwired (not required by brief's LINKS section).\n   - **Debug text unreadable**: first debug write produced a 58276px-wide unwrapped text → set textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\", resize(760,16), fontSize 14 for readable wrap.\n   - **get_screenshot timeouts**: occurred twice (debug node reads); both are retryable — one succeeded on retry, the most recent one (verifying move-trick) timed out and needs retry.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Established a reliable read-back channel (debug text node + node screenshot) since use_figma returns no values and get_design_context is unavailable. Reverse-engineered the actual reactions schema of this Figma API version through three diagnostic rounds (actions plural, DISSOLVE transitions required, destination must be non-ancestor top-level frame). Solved the self-referential logo link via the reparenting move-trick. All layout collapse issues resolved; both frames verified at 1440 wide with correct section structure. Prototype wiring completed for: 01_Work About nav→02_About, 02_About Work nav→01_Work, 02_About logo→01_Work, plus component-level hover states on Nav Link and Text Link masters (verified persisted from earlier call).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - “请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计： Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/4GPvqXGwp8Aaq4DfmSvw0k/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。”\n   - (Benchmark system constraints, preserve verbatim in effect: assigned file only; confirm assigned account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai via whoami; preserve all reference pages and their existing nodes; \"If an app name in the external query disagrees with this brief, use the product specified in 00 · Start Here\"; keep unrelated content intact; do not replace reference pages, create a different Figma file or switch accounts; use supplied Figma tools directly without delegating; unattended session — resolve routine choices using the brief; finish with the assigned file URL, the 03 · Workspace page ID, the screen IDs, the prototype work completed and any remaining limitations; every tool-call message needs a `Reasoning summary:` prefix; final answer format `Reasoning summary: ...` then `Final answer:`)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Retry get_screenshot of debug node 14:150 to verify the move-trick: expect `{\"set\":\"ok\",\"afterMove\":\"[{...destinationId 11:21...}]\",\"pos\":{...}}` — confirms Hotspot/Logo reaction survived the move into 11:21\n   - Delete debug node 14:150 (cleanup)\n   - Take full-frame screenshots of 01_Work (11:21) and 02_About (12:81) with enableBase64Response:true, maxDimension ~1500; visually inspect: header nav current states, display/hero typography, project block content, dividers, photo, skill lists, contact block, footer, hotspot invisibility\n   - Fix any visible problems found in screenshots; re-verify\n   - Write final answer: file URL https://www.figma.com/design/4GPvqXGwp8Aaq4DfmSvw0k/, page ID 4:2, frame IDs 11:21 (01_Work) + 12:81 (02_About) + component/master IDs, prototype summary (About nav→02_About; Work nav+logo on 02_About→01_Work; logo on 01_Work→01_Work via moved hotspot; hover variant-switching on all Nav Link and Text Link instances), limitations (Work nav self-click on 01_Work not wired — API rejects ancestor/self destinations, hover retained; scroll cue not clickable — destinations invalid per API and not required by brief's LINKS; image placeholders instead of real imagery per brief \"image placeholder\" requirement)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary: executed the move-trick workaround call — created a rectangle named \"Hotspot / Logo\" inside 02_About (12:81), set `hs.reactions=[{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"},actions:[{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:\"11:21\",navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3,easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}}]}]` (set succeeded per design, non-ancestor at set time), then `work.appendChild(hs); hs.layoutPositioning=\"ABSOLUTE\";` and positioned it over the Logo text inside the Header instance of 01_Work using `logo.absoluteBoundingBox` minus `work.absoluteBoundingBox` with 8px padding; wrote results (`out.set`, `out.afterMove` readback after move, `out.pos`) into debug node 14:150. Then attempted `get_screenshot` of node 14:150 (maxDimension 1200, enableBase64Response:true) to read the verification JSON — the call TIMED OUT with the retrya